{"type":"message","id":"f38d8b75","parentId":"84d964b8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T04:35:00.477Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the following tools available:\n\n- read: Read file contents\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- edit: Make precise edits to files\n- exec: Run shell commands (pty available for TTY-required CLIs)\n- process: Manage background exec sessions\n- web_search: Search the web using the configured provider\n- web_fetch: Fetch and extract readable content from a URL\n- sessions_list: List other sessions (incl. sub-agents) with filters/last\n- sessions_history: Fetch history for another session/sub-agent\n- sessions_yield: End this turn and wait for spawned sub-agent completion events\n- subagents: On-demand list/status visibility for sub-agent runs in this requester session; do not use for wait loops\n- session_status: Show a /status-equivalent status card (usage + time + Reasoning/Verbose/Elevated); use for model-use questions (📊 session_status); optional per-session model override\n- codemcp__find_symbol: Exact-match symbol lookup across the indexed repository\n- codemcp__get_file_context: Return all chunks for a given file plus the governing CLAUDE.md files\n- codemcp__list_commits: Enumerate indexed commit snapshots\n- codemcp__search_code: Semantic vector search over the indexed repository\n- fsmcp__edit_file: Replace an exact substring within an existing file\n- fsmcp__glob: Find files in the workspace by glob pattern\n- fsmcp__grep: Search file contents in the workspace using a JavaScript regular expression\n- fsmcp__list_dir: List the contents of a directory inside the workspace\n- fsmcp__read_file: Read a UTF-8 text file from the workspace\n- fsmcp__write_file: Create or overwrite a UTF-8 text file in the workspace\n- memory_get: Safe exact excerpt read from MEMORY.md or memory/*.md\n- memory_search: Semantically search MEMORY.md + memory/*.md before answering questions about prior work, decisions, dates, people, preferences, or todos\n- process: Manage running exec sessions for commands already started\n\nThese tools are designed to help with file operations, command execution, web interactions, session management, and more. Let me know how I can assist you further!"}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen2.5:7b","usage":{"input":9025,"output":462,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9487,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1780374900475}}
{"type":"message","id":"923155bc","parentId":"f38d8b75","timestamp":"2026-06-02T04:35:27.175Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Mon 2026-06-01 23:35 CDT] tell me about your architecture"}],"timestamp":1780374927174}}
{"type":"message","id":"0b23b98a","parentId":"923155bc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T04:35:40.729Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sure! Here’s an overview of the architecture for OpenClaw, focusing on its key components and design principles:\n\n### Architecture Overview\n\n#### Core Components:\n1. **Sub-Agents**: These are specialized agents that handle specific tasks such as coding, validating code changes, managing tools, and more.\n2. **Coordinator (You)**: This role coordinates the work by breaking down tasks into smaller chunks, spawning sub-agents for execution, and managing their output.\n\n#### Workflow:\n1. **Plan**: Break the task into manageable chunks and present a plan to the user.\n2. **Dispatch (Code)**: Spawn the CODER sub-agent to write or edit files.\n3. **Gather Evidence**: Read the changed files and any relevant caller/imported code after the CODER has completed.\n4. **Validate**: Spawn the VALIDATOR sub-agent to review the changes.\n5. **Decide**: Interpret the verdict from the validator to determine if the task is complete.\n\n#### Constraints:\n- Only one 14B model can be resident at a time, meaning you must manage the spawning and usage of sub-agents carefully.\n- The CODER cannot self-validate; it always sends changes to the VALIDATOR for review.\n\n### Key Roles:\n- **CODER**: Writes or edits files based on scoped prompts.\n- **VALIDATOR**: Reviews the coder’s work, providing a verdict (complete/incomplete/buggy).\n- **TOOLCHAIN**: Answers meta/utility queries about tools and models.\n\n#### File System Organization:\n- **AGENTS.md**: Defines roles and constraints for sub-agents.\n- **SOUL.md**: Contains persona/tone information.\n- **IDENTITY.md**, **USER.md**: Context files that may contain user-specific or system identity details (currently missing).\n\n### Tools and Their Use Cases:\n1. **codemcp__find_symbol**: Quickly locate symbols within the indexed repository.\n2. **fsmcp__edit_file**: Precisely edit a file by replacing exact substrings.\n3. **process**: Manage background processes for long-running commands or interactive sessions.\n4. **web_search** and **web_fetch**: Access web content for research or data collection.\n\n### Example Workflow:\n1. **Plan the Task**: Break down the task into smaller steps and present them to the user.\n2. **Spawn CODER Sub-Agent**: Provide a scoped prompt to the CODER sub-agent to make specific changes.\n3. **Read Changes**: After the CODER completes, read the modified files and any relevant callers/imported code.\n4. **Spawn VALIDATOR Sub-Agent**: Send the coder’s summary, diffs, and relevant file contents for review.\n5. **Interpret Verdict**: Based on the validator's response, determine if the task is complete or needs further action.\n\n### Constraints:\n- Never edit files yourself; always delegate to CODER.\n- Avoid spawning two 14B sub-agents in parallel.\n- Ensure you have approval from the user before retrying a failed task.\n\nThis architecture ensures that tasks are broken down into manageable parts, validated for correctness, and leverages specialized sub-agents for different roles. If you have any specific questions or need further details on any aspect, feel free to ask!"}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen2.5:7b","usage":{"input":9501,"output":657,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10158,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1780374940727}}
